  "equipment_type": "Commercial boiler / water heater / pool heater controller",
  "applies_to": "Lochinvar Copper-fin II/IIE boilers and water heaters (models 402-2072) and pool heaters (502-2072) with the SMART SYSTEM control.",
  "summary": "Copper-fin II/IIE units expose BACnet MS/TP through Lochinvar's optional Modbus/BACnet communication board. The map follows the same pattern as the other SMART SYSTEM appliances: stage enables and a tank thermostat as BVs, safety and output status as BIs, temperatures and status/blocking/lockout codes as AIs, and BAS-written commands and temperatures as AVs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "Base + MAC address; the manual's example base is 620000 (base is model dependent and can be changed)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The BACnet board is an MS/TP master; MAC addresses 0-127 are set on dip switches 1-7.",
    "AV 0 (Configuration) is a bitmask telling the control which values the BAS will supply; AV 1 carries the BV 0-4 command bits as one word.",
    "AI 0-2 are the binary inputs packed into 16-bit words.",
    "Stage enables BV 1-3 apply to multi-stage boilers controlled per stage (Control Mode 2).",
    "Temperatures are in °C on the bus; Rev F adds a °F option on dip switch 8 of the board.",
    "Cascade totals are only seen on the leader; fit a board to each unit to see its own values."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set parameter H6 ModBus to Active so the control accepts BAS commands, then write AV 0 Configuration with the bits for the values the BAS will supply. The BAS then sends the enable (BV 0 or the AV 1 word), and optionally a rate or setpoint on AV 2 (H3 BMS input Active) and a tank setpoint on AV 3. Commands must be refreshed; monitoring needs no setup.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "why": "Bitmask of BAS-supplied inputs; resend before commands",
        "name": "Configuration"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 0",
        "why": "Enable / call for heat from the BAS",
        "name": "Stage 1 Enable"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "why": "Rate command: firing % or setpoint, per BMS Type",
        "name": "0 - 10V Inp. / Rate Cmd / Setp. Cmd"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 13",
        "why": "What the unit is doing",
        "name": "Status Code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 8",
        "why": "Outlet water temperature, °C",
        "name": "Outlet Temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 11",
        "why": "Burner firing rate, %",
        "name": "Firing Rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 15",
        "why": "Lockout cause",
        "name": "Lockout Code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set H6 ModBus = Active. Control Mode 1: enable (BV 0) and/or tank thermostat (BV 4) with local setpoints. Mode 2: each stage enabled directly after H5 Sequencer = Active (boilers only). Mode 3: enable plus a % rate on AV 2 with H3 BMS input = Active. Mode 4: enable plus setpoint via AV 2 (J1 BMS Type = Set point) and/or AV 3 tank/pool setpoint. Mode 5: AV 2 alone acts as enable and rate/setpoint with H2 Enable input = Inactive. Write the matching AV 0 bits first in each mode.",
    "heartbeat": "BAS-supplied system/tank temperatures and the 0-10 V value must be updated within the H7 timeout (1-255 s, default 10 s) or the control reverts to its own readings. Other commands have a fixed 4-minute timeout; if not refreshed the unit runs on its own inputs.",
    "remote_sensors": "Set the AV 0 bits, then write AV 4 tank temperature, AV 5 outdoor temperature, AV 6 system supply or AV 7 pool/system return temperature in °C. Rewrite them faster than the H7 timeout.",
    "setup": [
      "MAC address from dip switches 1-7 (0-127); baud from switches 9-10: 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800.",
      "Device instance = base + MAC; the base can be changed (0-4194048) and reset by powering up with switches 1-8 on.",
      "Default device name is \"MTR-01 BACnet\".",
      "Board LED D7: 1 s bright / 1 s dim = normal; 1.5 s on / 0.5 s off = no BACnet communication."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The manual says to resend the AV 0 configuration bits before each command.",
      "AV 2 is a 0-100 % image of the 0-10 V input; as a setpoint it is scaled between the BMS temperatures at low and high input.",
      "Writing 0 to the AV 1 command word disables the unit."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
    "title": "Copper-fin II/IIE Boiler, Water Heater and Pool Heater ModBus and BACnet Communication Instructions",
